      "side": 1,
      "message": "You need to add this here as well:\n\n```\n\tif (p3s_4k_unsupported(vma-\u003evm_mm))\n\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n```\n\nThe reason is because when a 4KB process calls mmap() on an io_uring fd       __get_unmapped_area() invokes file-\u003ef_op-\u003eget_unmapped_area (io_uring_get_unmapped_area()) before mmap_region() ever calls file-\u003ef_op-\u003emmap (io_uring_mmap()). This leads to io_uring_get_unmapped_area() returning -ENOMEM or -EINVAL instead of -ENOTSUPP.",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "d1ea493d_b87e9da3",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "io_uring/memmap.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 1,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 1,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\tif (p3s_4k_unsupported(current-\u003emm))\n\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
